{
  "_comment": [
    "Trick shot challenges, loaded by modes/trick_shots.py.",
    "",
    "Positions are in TABLE INCHES on a 7 ft playing surface (76 x 38), with the",
    "origin at the inside of the top-left cushion, +x along the long axis. They",
    "are rescaled proportionally for a different table size, so a challenge",
    "authored here plays the same on a 9 ft table.",
    "",
    "The spec's example file used pixel coordinates. Pixels are a property of",
    "the camera mount, not of the shot, so the same file would describe a",
    "different challenge on every installation -- and would stop being valid the",
    "moment somebody nudged the camera.",
    "",
    "Fields: id, name, description (projected verbatim, keep it under ~50 chars),",
    "difficulty 1-3, balls (cue first), target_pocket, and the optional",
    "requirements min_rails / min_potted that decide the third star."
  ],
